[1m[95m[NARRATION][0m 
  Mara Venn straightens from where she leans against the bar, a tin cup of 
  something dark cradled between her fingers. The copper lamps throw shifting 
  light across her charcoal coat. She doesn't return the greeting. Instead, she 
  watches you for a long moment — measuring. "Kael." A nod. Then she sets the 
  cup down and jerks her chin toward the shuttered window. The Ash Gate side. 
  "Learned enough to know I was right to come find you first." She pulls a 
  folded scrap of paper from her coat pocket and flattens it on the scarred 
  tabletop. A rough sketch — the Gate's archway, notations in cramped script 
  along the margins. "Old Bram's skiff was found tied to the south pier at 
  dusk. No sign of him. No blood. No struggle." She taps the sketch. "The 
  Gate's seal was intact when I arrived. But the ashes around the base — 
  they're disturbed. Fresh footprints leading *in*. Not out." Her eyes lift to 
  yours. "Someone crossed three nights ago. And whoever they are, they didn't 
  come back." She waits. The tavern creaks. A log settles in the hearth. "What 
  do you make of that?" 

