[1m[95m[NARRATION][0m 
  The rain picks up, drumming harder against the shutters. Mara's hand hovers 
  over the compass — still not taking it. Then she does something unexpected. 
  She pulls off her left glove. The motion is slow, deliberate. The leather 
  peels away, and beneath it — across the back of her hand, curving from 
  knuckle to wrist — is a scar. Pale, puckered, fresh. A crescent shape, as 
  though something with a curved blade caught her and *held*. She holds her 
  hand out, palm open, so you can see it clearly in the lamplight. "This is 
  what I found when I followed the footprints to the Gate's threshold." Her jaw 
  tightens. "Something reached *through* the seal, Kael. Not a hand. Not a 
  claw. Something that shouldn't exist on this side of the stone." She looks at 
  you, and the measuring distance in her eyes is gone. Replaced by something 
  harder. Something *committed*. "I came here to find answers. But I came here 
  alone because I didn't trust anyone else to survive the looking." She flexes 
  her scarred hand. "You handed me your family's compass without a second 
  thought. That's not the act of a man who walks away." She takes the compass. 
  Her fingers close around it, and she tucks it into an inner pocket of her 
  charcoal coat. "Then we're in this together." Her voice is quiet, final. 
  "Whatever came through that Gate, whoever crossed three nights ago — we find 
  them. We expose what's behind it. And we don't stop until the Ash Gate's 
  secrets are ash themselves." She meets your eyes. "Sworn." A beat of silence. 
  The hearth pops. "Now. What do you want to know first?" 

