[1m[95m[NARRATION][0m 
  Mara holds your gaze for a long moment after the vow settles between you. 
  Then, slowly, she reaches into her inner pocket. The compass comes back out. 
  She doesn't place it on the table. She holds it — a beat longer than 
  necessary — then extends it toward you, lanyard dangling. "I took it to keep 
  it safe," she says. "But I've been thinking since the words left my mouth. If 
  we're sworn to this — if we're walking into whatever's behind that Gate 
  together — then that compass isn't a burden I carry for you." Her fingers 
  brush yours as you close your hand around the familiar brass casing. "It's a 
  *tool*. And you might need it faster than I can pass it back." She releases 
  it. The weight settles into your palm, warm from her coat. "I'll still guard 
  it with my life. But it stays in *your* hands until we cross that threshold." 
  She pulls her glove back on, working the leather tight over the crescent 
  scar. "You ready to see the Gate up close?" 
